WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.404
Preparation happens before the alert that everyone remembers.

2
00:00:03.554 --> 00:00:09.937
It is the quiet work that makes the rest of incident response possible: assigning roles,

3
00:00:10.087 --> 00:00:18.598
defining escalation paths, maintaining playbooks, confirming tool access, checking log availability, testing backups, and making sure decision makers can be

4
00:00:18.748 --> 00:00:20.948
reached.

5
00:00:21.098 --> 00:00:27.906
Preparation also includes legal, privacy, communications, and business-owner coordination, because many incidents are not purely technical.

6
00:00:28.056 --> 00:00:34.865
A suspicious login may affect an employee account, a cloud credential exposure may involve customer data,

7
00:00:35.015 --> 00:00:38.845
and a system outage may require business continuity decisions.

8
00:00:38.995 --> 00:00:46.229
The team should know who can approve containment, who can contact vendors, who can speak to leadership,

9
00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.932
and where evidence should be stored.

10
00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:55.465
Tabletop exercises and drills are useful because they expose gaps before a real incident does.

11
00:00:55.615 --> 00:01:00.296
A playbook that has never been tested is only a theory.

12
00:01:00.446 --> 00:01:06.829
Readiness means people understand their role, monitoring provides useful context, backups can actually be restored,

13
00:01:06.979 --> 00:01:09.957
and communication paths work when time matters.

14
00:01:10.107 --> 00:01:16.916
Good preparation lowers confusion, shortens response time, and gives responders confidence that they can act safely.

15
00:01:17.066 --> 00:01:24.726
A practical readiness review should also check boring details that become critical later: who can approve emergency access,

16
00:01:24.876 --> 00:01:33.386
where bridge notes are kept, which logs are retained long enough, and how the team reaches a vendor or cloud

17
00:01:33.536 --> 00:01:35.736
provider after hours.

18
00:01:35.886 --> 00:01:40.567
Preparation turns those details into known paths instead of last-minute discoveries.
